# KDE Plasma 6 Wayland Suite — Cursor CLI Rules

You have access to the `kde-wayland-suite` in this repository.

When the user asks about keyboard layouts (ABNT2, US-intl, cedilla), broken shortcuts (Ctrl+C), or touchpad gestures in KDE Plasma 6 Wayland:

1. To run a full diagnostic:
   execute `./bin/kde-config status` or `make check`
2. To fix keyboard shortcuts and configure XCompose cedilla:
   execute `./bin/kde-config fix-keyboard` or `make fix-keyboard`
3. To configure touchpad gestures (libinput-gestures):
   execute `./bin/kde-config gestures` or `make gestures`
4. To switch active keyboard layout:
   execute `./bin/kde-config switch br` or `./bin/kde-config switch us`
